\f1\fs22 	The work on the disc will proceed to the point that they have decoded a few messages - \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		Mostly desperate pleas or recording the entire aggregate knowledge of the civilization. (Music, Art, history, science, memes - everything ever recorded.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		The \'93other\'94 earths are almost exactly the same, some divergence in political landscapes, names of countries (USA = UACS) (PTD = Eastern Australia) (Vietnesia = China) and leaders (Trump = Dunning Kruger), but fundamentally similar.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		With the exception of their own earth which is different is a few fundamental ways \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		All other earths only have one Elvis who had a stellar albiet short career. (Compare names of songs Kentucky Rain? Love me Tender? (The High Elvis will not be impressed and will ridicule the lack of science and reason in the songs - No songs about evolution? What was he thinking? And those Elvis movies are just awful - I would never stoop so low.)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		There is no equivalent Richard Dawkins clone at the time of the crunch, but some of the other players are represented in the other universes - Sarah, Johnny, CEO (Prime Minister), Hayley, Damien Hardman and on each and every occasion, no matter what they did, they could not stop the universe from collapsing in on itself. (Alway preceded by o the discovery of the gyges discs) The PTD universe is different and they have a degree of hope that they may be able to stop the cycle of universes being destroyed and other universes popping into existence.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		It would seem that the conditions precedent for the end of the universe -Discovery of the Discs once the Discs are discovered/created annihilation is inevitable. All who have tried to stop the inevitability have failed. But they have the Dawkins and the Elvi Nation.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		Initial attempts to download the information, crashes the computer capacity of the lab and the information was lost. The information is dumped at once, sort of a zip file with the information enclosed in packets of data once opened.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		Have to use the quatum bio-processors of the Hardy control centre as they have the capacity to handle the data, but the memory of the computer has to be all but wiped or transferred to another site.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		For the system to handle the information, Richard has to act as a biological buffer for serialising and marshalling the vast information dump.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		Some sort of double dealing with Eloise to use her computers to dump the finance database to her computers. She will think she has got control, but when she tries to fire it up, she will discover that she cannot open the system without DNA key code. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		When the transfer happens Richard will be wired to the system with from various contact points on his head.He tells them not to stop the transfer no matter what. Stopping mid stream could pop him out of existence or he could possibly jump time lines. The transfer is slow at first and then he begins to glow, low at first, but as he glows brighter the data transfer rate increases and he glows brighter and brighter. Gravity seems to increase and the become heavier and heavier. Furniture begins to buckle and squish diagonally down towards the bunker. They all begin to freak out and big debate as to whether to stop. Eventually Johnny tries and fighting against the gravity he almost hits the \'93stop\'94 button - somehow thwarted.\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		Richard finally glows less and less until you can see him - a grown man in his mid 20\'92s. Due to time dilation it was only 10minutes for the occupants of the bunker but 20 years for Richard. Q\'92s about how? \'93My brain had to grow (evolve) to cope with the data and the nature of the gravity well slowed down time for him and he had time to process the information. He \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		When the fridge guys arrive they are aghast. \'93Do you know what could have happened if you spin the dics? You could have collapsed the entire universe. How It did not happen is impossible!\'94 \'93Maybe we are all dead\'94 said Cracker. Richard, now a full grown adult confirms Cracker\'92s idea of inoculating one with the Panacea virus and one with the Panacea Anti-virus proves to be correct and the transfer is successful. \
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		Johnny gets dealt with - no acknowledgement of any part of the discovery of multi-verses (or a series of big-bang/big crunch universes)\
{\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>		The information is vast but all earths end the same way. The discovery of the discs always precede the eventual demise of the universe, just the amount of time it takes differs. The player are pretty much the same in the other multi-verses, but in the PTD there is an extra character - The Dawkins - they a are involved with the examination of the discs in the PTD. \
